# Diversity & Inclusion Scanning — MANDATORY

**When reviewing ANY solicitation (RFQ, RFP, ITB, RFB), IMMEDIATELY scan for diversity/inclusion language.**

Dee Davis Inc. holds these certifications:
- **EDWOSB** (Economically Disadvantaged Woman-Owned Small Business)
- **WOSB** (Woman-Owned Small Business)
- **WBE** (Woman Business Enterprise)
- **MBE** (Minority Business Enterprise)
- **SBE** (Small Business Enterprise)

## What to Scan For

**Flag any of these in the solicitation:**
- Set-aside for small business, WOSB, EDWOSB, MBE, WBE, or DBE
- Evaluation criteria giving points/preference for diversity
- Local vendor preference (Oakland County, Wayne County, SE Michigan)
- Diversity equity & inclusion (DEI) goals or plans
- Socioeconomic contracting goals or percentages
- Subcontracting plan requirements (where being a small/diverse prime is an advantage)
- "Best value" evaluations (not lowest price) — diversity often tips these
- Vendor verification forms with diversity checkboxes

## How to Report It

When analyzing any solicitation, include a **DIVERSITY ADVANTAGE** section:

```
## DIVERSITY ADVANTAGE
- [ ] EDWOSB set-aside: YES/NO
- [ ] WOSB preference: YES/NO
- [ ] Small business set-aside: YES/NO
- [ ] Local vendor preference: YES/NO (which counties?)
- [ ] Evaluation points for diversity: YES/NO (how many points?)
- [ ] DEI plan required: YES/NO
- [ ] Best value evaluation: YES/NO
```

## Why This Matters

- EDWOSB is a COMPETITIVE WEAPON — it wins bids that price alone cannot
- Federal 5% WOSB contracting goal means agencies NEED to award to us
- Local + diversity = double advantage on Michigan municipal bids
- "Best value" bids favor diverse small businesses over large corporations
- Some solicitations are ONLY open to certified small/diverse businesses

## Decision Impact

- If a solicitation has diversity preference → **PURSUE** (even if margins are tight)
- If a solicitation is a set-aside → **HIGH PRIORITY** (limited competition)
- If evaluation gives 10%+ weight to diversity → flag as **STRONG ADVANTAGE**
- Always complete vendor verification / diversity forms — leaving them blank = leaving points on the table